# ============================================================================
# BRINEHAVEN  (harbor town, 20x20 blocks, buffer 676/1300)  johto_modern
# ============================================================================
# HOOK: Silkwater's two canals drain into Brinehaven's harbor; it is the
#   ferry port to the Orange Islands (M3) and the busiest wharf in Johto.
#   The town is laid out in strips between the canals: Upper Town (homes,
#   PC, Mart, the Harbor Master's tower), the Wharf (warehouses, ferry
#   terminal, the railed ferry pier) and the Fish Market strip with a
#   railed fishing pier. East and south edges are open sea (Surf routes).
#
# BUILDINGS (door steps in obj warp lines)
#   PC, Mart, small home                       Upper Town, NW
#   Harbor Master's Tower (2x3 radio-tower art) Upper Town; gives the
#     Warehouse Key after the smuggling quest, sells ferry tickets
#   Sailor's house, Seafarer's Inn (3x2)        Upper Town, NE
#   Fishermen's Guild (3x2)                     Old Rod / fishing tips
#   Warehouses 1 and 2 (brown roofs)            Wharf; 2 holds items/trainers
#   Ferry Terminal (3x2)                        Wharf; ticket gate -> pier
#   Fish Market (4x2, brown roofs; the 2b/2c half is a sealed loading bay)
#   Net-mender's house                          Fish Market strip
#
# GAMEPLAY BEATS
#   1. Walk in from Silkwater along the brick Wharf Road (W exit rows 10-11).
#   2. Ferry blocked: "sailings suspended" -- crates going missing.
#   3. A fisherman on the fishing pier saw Rockets using the fish market's
#      sealed loading bay; Harbor Master hands over the key; Warehouse 2 /
#      Fish Market interior is a short Rocket hideout (2-3 grunts).
#   4. Ferry resumes: sailor at the ferry pier tip warps you to the boat.
#   5. With Surf: east/south sea routes, the canals back to Silkwater,
#      hidden items on the pier tips' water side.
#
# CONNECTIONS: W edge lines up with Silkwater's E edge row-for-row (canals
#   on rows 7-8 and 14-15, road on rows 10-11, trees elsewhere). N exit (cols
#   3-4) to a coastal route. E and S edges are sea.
# TILE GAPS: no ship/ferry hull blocks (use the Fast Ship gangway as a
#   sprite or add a block); no wooden-pier block, piers are pavement with
#   61/43 railings; no bottom-shore water, so pier tips end on a 46 rail.
# ============================================================================
tileset johto_modern
ref GoldenrodCity
key T=05 .=01 :=06 ,=02 *=04 h=67 o=0a ~=35 n=43 u=61 [=58 ]=59 v=76 %=36 $=34
key <=44 >=46 s=45 S=77 w=66
key R=18 M=1f N=19 A=10 D=17 Z=11 E=1a P=1b O=16 W=1e K=33 1=14 2=13 9=08 0=09 b=2b c=2c
key i=25 m=2e y=29 q=2a d=2d
grid:
TTT..TTTTTTTTTTTTTTT
TRN..RMN..im.RNRMNTT
TEP..ADK..yq.OWADZTT
T.........dm.......T
T.RMN.,*,s..h...h..T
T.ADZ.12..h...nnnnnn
T.............[~~$~~
nnnn<>nnnn<>nn~~~~~~
uuuu<>uuuu<>uu~~~~~~
T.90.90..RMN..[~~~~~
..OW.OW..ADZ..uuuuu~
::::::::::::::....>~
T.h..h........nnnnn~
T...w......w..[~~%~~
nnnnnnn<>nnnnn~~~~~~
uuuuuuu<>uuuuu~~~~~~
T.9090...RN.h.[~~~~~
T.OWbc...OW.h.uuuu~~
TS::::::::::::....>~
TTTTTTTTTTTTTTnnnnn~
end
exit W 0 21
exit N 6 0
exit PokeCenter 3 5
exit Mart 12 5
exit HarborMaster 21 7
exit Sailor 27 5
exit Inn 32 5
exit HouseNW 13 11
exit FishGuild 6 11
exit Warehouse1 5 21
exit Warehouse2 11 21
exit Ferry 20 21
exit FishMarket 5 35
exit NetMender 19 35
exit FerryTip 35 22
exit SeaE 39 14
